# Original project pattern: six-sided cluster motif
title: Hexagon cluster motif (6-fold)
terms: US
yarn: dk-3
hook: 4.0mm
params: dk-3_4.0mm
source: original (written for this project, 2026)
license: CC0-1.0
notes: A hexagon worked from a magic ring, with 3-dc clusters at the six corners and 2-dc groups along the sides, finished with an sc round (the ch-1 side spaces are passed over, not filled) with picots at the corners and mid-sides. Design intent: a joinable hexagon for blankets, but here a single motif. Exercises magic ring, beginning cluster ("ch 2, 2-dc cl in same sp"), cluster pairs in a corner space, side groups, travelling by slip stitches into a space, and picots. Real hexagons lie flat; NOTE the analytic flatness check treats rounds as circles, so a 6-fold cornered motif will read as slightly "over" at the corners.

Rnd 1: mr, ch 3 (counts as dc), dc in ring, ch 2, *2 dc in ring, ch 2* x5, join. (12 dc, 6 ch-2 sps)
Rnd 2: sl st in next st, sl st in next ch-2 sp, ch 2, 2-dc cl in same sp, ch 3, 3-dc cl in same sp, ch 2, *(3-dc cl, ch 3, 3-dc cl) in next ch-2 sp, ch 2* x5, join. (12 cl, 6 ch-3 sps, 6 ch-2 sps)
Rnd 3: sl st in next ch-3 sp, ch 2, 2-dc cl in same sp, ch 3, 3-dc cl in same sp, ch 1, 3 dc in next ch-2 sp, ch 1, *(3-dc cl, ch 3, 3-dc cl) in next ch-3 sp, ch 1, 3 dc in next ch-2 sp, ch 1* x5, join. (12 cl, 18 dc, 6 ch-3 sps, 12 ch-1 sps)
Rnd 4: sl st in next ch-3 sp, ch 2, 2-dc cl in same sp, ch 3, 3-dc cl in same sp, ch 1, (3 dc in next ch-1 sp, ch 1) x2, *(3-dc cl, ch 3, 3-dc cl) in next ch-3 sp, ch 1, (3 dc in next ch-1 sp, ch 1) x2* x5, join. (12 cl, 36 dc, 6 ch-3 sps, 18 ch-1 sps)
Rnd 5: ch 1, sc in same st, (2 sc, picot, 2 sc) in next ch-3 sp, sc in next st, sc in next 3 sts, picot, sc in next 3 sts, *sc in next st, (2 sc, picot, 2 sc) in next ch-3 sp, sc in next st, sc in next 3 sts, picot, sc in next 3 sts* x5, join, fasten off. (72 sc, 12 picot)
